          "description": {
            "comment": "Methanothermobacter marburgensis strain Marburg is a hydrogenotrophic methanogen in the archaeal domain. It grows thermophilically and anaerobically, and was first isolated from an anaerobic sewage digestor in Marburg, Germany (Fuchs et al., 1978). This sample was inoculated using a pure culture from the DSMZ (DSM 2133). It cultured on H2 (80%) and CO2 (20%) in MS media (Balch et al. 1979, modified Sarbu 2013) at 65C in serum bottles. The genomic DNA was then extracted and used for genome sequencing and assembly.",
